# CHANGES.log — enerlytics-lp-redesign

## 2026-09-04 (v4.1) · founder fixes
- Chapter I heat map replaced by the ORIGINAL site's calendar (one square per day, navy→blue→amber ramp,
  live year-to-date meter), now coloured by cost with summer weekdays priced at the day-peak band.
- "Across sites" map beat removed from Control it (solar + storage); the map stays in Every facility.
- Every facility: "Who we build for" — eight client-type tiles with icons under the map.

## 2026-09-04 (v4) · evidence instead of slogans

Founder on v3: chapter I too much jargon ("every hour has its own price…") → a heat map; the anomaly
chapter overlapped the cycle and its photo said nothing about money → simpler, quantified; Control it
should drop the "peak" beat and show assets in different locations; lists of names over photos = the
poorest thing.
- film/why-now.tsx → tariff cost heat map (12 months × 24 h, amber = money) with two facts:
  summer-afternoon share of cost vs share of hours. Plain language, no slogans.
- film/price-it.tsx → anomaly detection + predictive maintenance as one drift chart: efficiency
  vs the asset's own baseline over 12 weeks, flagged in week 3, amber area = money leaving, two
  numbers (caught early OMR 340 vs found at failure OMR 20,195; illustrative). No ladder, no photo.
- film/site-map.tsx + lib/gulf-map.ts → Oman outline (johan/world.geo.json, public domain) with
  sites as lit points, per-site reading/state, portfolio totals. Used in Control it (new "Across
  sites" beat replacing "Peak") and Every facility (replacing the typographic list).
- film/company.tsx → "why defensible" as three concrete columns instead of one line on a photo.


## 2026-09-04 (v3) · substance back into the film

Founder on v2: "feels like an AI slide ppt — what happened to the services, the six-stage cycle,
the assets?" Fix: keep the cinema, restore the objects, vary the compositions.
- components/film/cycle-scene.tsx — the six-stage cycle as the signature object: a pinned wheel
  over the night aerial that rotates with scroll, arcs lighting in order, feedback arc at stage 6,
  full stage copy (question / body / output / owner) in systems language. Nav anchor #how.
- components/film/see-it.tsx — assets as an editorial filmstrip: five tall frames (cooling,
  electrical, solar, storage, grid) from the site's own plates, each with a reading and a state.
- components/film/chapter-marker.tsx replaces full-screen title cards (the slide-deck cadence).
- components/services.tsx restored from git (light, calm) inside chapter VI after the
  software/engineer table. Mobile scrim on PlateStory for legibility.


## 2026-09-04 (later) · redesign/cinematic v2 — "the film" (CMO cut)

Founder verdict on v1: 5.5/10 — one image is not cinema; do not mirror the MVP's parts list;
sell the vision to investors and clients; look at film-title sites. Treatment: docs/TREATMENT_v2.md.

### Added
- components/film/: cold-open, why-now, see-it, understand-it (with the cycle), price-it,
  control-it, prove-it, every-facility, company; plate-story (sticky plate + scrolling
  statements), title-card (roman-numeral chapter cards, letterboxed).
- components/cinematic/depth-plate.tsx: WebGL depth-parallax for stills (60-line shader,
  scroll + pointer driven, poster fallback). assets-src/depth.py: Depth Anything V2 (small),
  run locally on CPU → public/media/<id>-depth.jpg (6–14 KB each).
- Five new plates via Codex: h09 transmission tower, h10 meter macro, h11 dawn aerial,
  (h07 engineer / h08 rooftop pending), depth maps for all served plates.
- Nav = chapter index (See it · Understand it · Price it · Control it · Prove it · Company).

### Changed
- Copy now speaks in systems (cooling, electrical, process loads, solar, storage, grid) —
  no chillers/compressors/AHUs/approach-temperature on the marketing site.
- Vision line: "The operating intelligence layer for physical energy." Investor arc explicit
  (why now → what we see → how it pays → where it goes → why defensible → how big → who).
- Services folded into chapter VI (Prove it) as one line; asset graph and dashboards removed.

### Removed
v1 chapters hero-scene, peak-cost, asset-graph, anomaly-scene, portfolio-scene, closing-scene,
the-loop (replaced by the compact cycle in chapter III), services.


